---
description: eZsign brand and visual rules — apply when writing any prototype UI
globs: prototypes/**,blueprint/patterns/**
alwaysApply: false
---

Before writing UI, read `blueprint/brand/brand.md`.

Tokens: `blueprint/tokens/ez-tokens.css` (primitives `--prim-*` + semantics, shared with the mono) and `blueprint/tokens/components.css` (component knobs). Semantic names are `{role}-{modifier}`: roles `background surface foreground border accent overlay focus positive negative warning info`, modifiers `-muted -subtle -strong -inverse -foreground`. Hover/pressed states are not tokens: `color-mix()` in the component. There is a dark theme (`.body--dark`, Quasar's class): the same names change value, so a prototype that only uses semantic tokens works in both — never test the theme, never use `dark:`. In prototypes:
- ✅ Semantic utilities: `bg-surface`, `bg-background`, `bg-surface-muted`, `text-foreground`, `text-foreground-muted`, `text-foreground-subtle`, `text-accent`, `border-border`, `border-border-subtle`, `bg-positive-subtle`, `text-negative-strong`… and `var(--color-…)` in scoped styles.
- ✅ Tailwind layout/spacing utilities (`flex`, `gap-3`, `grid`, `p-4`, `text-sm`, `font-semibold`…).
- ❌ Raw colors (hex, rgb, hsl, named), `--prim-*`, Tailwind palette (`bg-blue-500` — disabled), arbitrary color values (`text-[#…]`).
- ⚠ Avoid arbitrary pixel values and inline styles; use component props and tokens.

Visual principles:
- One `primary` button per zone. Others `secondary` or `flat`. Destructive = `danger`.
- Status always as `ez-badge` with the object's `stateTone()` / `stateLabel()`: same status, same color everywhere.
- White surfaces on the pale canvas, cards grouped in sections. No gradients, strong shadows or decorative illustrations.
- Numbers and dates right-aligned in tables.
- Empty states have a title, a sentence and, when possible, the action to get out of them.
